{"source_id":"arXiv:1404.6879","title":"\\LargeQuantization of the shift of argument subalgebras in type $A$","abstract":"Given a simple Lie algebra $\\mathfrak{g}$ and an element $μ\\in\\mathfrak{g}^*$, the corresponding shift of argument subalgebra of $\\text{S}(\\mathfrak{g})$ is Poisson commutative. In the case where $μ$ is regular, this subalgebra is known to admit a quantization, that is, it can be lifted to a commutative subalgebra of $\\text{U}(\\mathfrak{g})$. We show that if $\\mathfrak{g}$ is of type $A$, then this property extends to arbitrary $μ$, thus proving a conjecture of Feigin, Frenkel and Toledano Laredo. The proof relies on an explicit construction of generators of the center of the affine vertex algebra at the critical level.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Alexander Molev"],"year":"2014","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.6879","doi":"10.48550/arXiv.1404.6879","cluster":"representation_theory","cards":[{"card_id":"ma-c-6f9d94bc3d68ec817b0b","label":"Abstract","kind":"abstract","line":191,"snippet":"Given a simple Lie algebra $\\g$ and an element $\\mu\\in\\g^*$, the corresponding shift of argument subalgebra of $\\Sr(\\g)$ is Poisson commutative. In the case where $\\mu$ is regular, this subalgebra is …"}],"conclusions_only":false,"held":1,"macros":{"End":"{\\rm{End}\\ts}","Hom":"{\\rm{Hom}}","Mat":"{\\rm{Mat}}","ad":"{\\rm{ad}\\ts}","ch":"{\\rm{ch}\\ts}","chara":"{\\rm{char}\\ts}","ind":"{\\rm{ind}\\ts}","diag":"{\\rm diag}","pr":"^{\\tss\\prime}","non":"\\nonumber","wt":"\\widetilde","wh":"\\widehat","ot":"\\otimes","la":"\\lambda","ls":"\\ts\\lambda\\ts","La":"\\Lambda","De":"\\Delta","al":"\\alpha","be":"\\beta","ga":"\\gamma","Ga":"\\Gamma","ep":"\\epsilon","ka":"\\kappa","vk":"\\varkappa","vt":"\\vartheta","si":"\\sigma","vp":"\\varphi","de":"\\delta","ze":"\\zeta","om":"\\omega","ee":"\\epsilon^{}","su":"s^{}","hra":"\\hookrightarrow","ve":"\\varepsilon","ts":"\\,","vac":"\\mathbf{1}","di":"\\partial","qin":"q^{-1}","tss":"\\hspace{1pt